1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:05,246
Which document should rank higher: one ranked
first by keyword search and fifth by

2
00:00:05,246 --> 00:00:08,850
vector search, or one ranked second
by vector search only?

3
00:00:09,850 --> 00:00:15,687
Reciprocal rank fusion adds one over 60 plus
the rank, for each list a document

4
00:00:15,687 --> 00:00:16,500
appears in.

5
00:00:17,117 --> 00:00:20,892
First and fifth scores about 0.0318.

6
00:00:21,192 --> 00:00:25,967
Second in one list only
scores about 0.0161.

7
00:00:26,267 --> 00:00:28,867
Agreement between retrievers wins.

8
00:00:29,883 --> 00:00:36,553
It uses ranks, not raw scores, so you never
have to normalize BM25 against cosine

9
00:00:36,553 --> 00:00:37,458
similarity.

10
00:00:37,758 --> 00:00:39,958
That's why it's the right default.

11
00:00:40,983 --> 00:00:44,208
The full guide to hybrid
search is on vidyal.ai.
